Over the summer of 2025, I spent just over a month working at a startup called
Malcolm, which describes itself as "A unified data architecture for alternative 
investment funds." When I began working, the startup was just getting off the ground,
and the team was relatively small. As such, I gained a large amount of useful
experience working on a tight-knit team, and was deeply involved with creating our
initial product to show to potential companies which would want to deal with us.

I am also a musician, and playing a musical instrument has deeply influenced my
attitudes towards problem solving. I play in my school's orchestra as a first violin,
frequently playing parts which go up to and exceed grade 8 standard. I have been
playing for nearly thirteen years, and I have learned to take my time working through
difficult passages, and think critically about each movement and adjustment I make to
playing a piece well. This, in turn, has helped me with my ability to solve problems
